ur skills.","stem":"Skill used | What I did / found | How trustworthy? (evidence)","lookFor":"Completed verification and risk mitigation on the Log, with evidence, plus reflection across the four skills - data quality, prompt refinement, data influence, and verification/risk. Mastery reflection also names a next step; partial reflects on some skills only.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CU·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·SD·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":4,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CE·G4·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·GE·G5·A"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"advanced"},{"id":"g6-bridging-w6-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Exit ticket: state whether your helper can be trusted and give two reasons (one verification, one risk mitigation).","lookFor":"States a judgement on whether the helper can be trusted and gives two reasons, one verification and one risk mitigation.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CU·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·SD·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":4,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CE·G4·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·GE·G5·A"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"advanced"},{"id":"g6-bridging-w6-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"prompt":"Challenge (stretch): your helper is safe for one use but risky for another. Explain the difference and propose a rule for when it should and should not be used.","lookFor":"Weighs a fairness/safety trade-off: distinguishes the safe use from the risky one and proposes a workable rule for when the helper should and should not be used.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CU·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·SD·G5·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":4,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·CE·G4·A"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":5,"tier":"A","code":"AIF·GE·G5·A"}],"evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"advanced"}]}},"g6-main-w1-core":{"id":"g6-main-w1-core","number":1,"week":1,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Unit Launch - Rule-Based vs Learning Systems","summary":"Students meet the term's big question by sorting three real systems into 'follows fixed rules' or 'learns from data', posting their own questions and helping agree the class responsible-use rules.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Generate at least two questions about how rule-based and learning systems differ.","Classify three systems as 'follows fixed rules' or 'learns from data', justifying each.","Co-construct the unit success criteria and the responsible-use norms for AI tools."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Some machines are told every single step. Others are shown lots of examples and work out the pattern themselves. This term you become a system detective - can you tell which kind you are looking at?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can ask at least two genuine questions about rule-based and learning systems.","I can sort three systems into 'follows fixed rules' or 'learns from data' and give a reason for each.","I can help write our class responsible-use rules for AI tools."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"rule-based system","definition":"A system that follows fixed steps a person wrote for it."},{"term":"learning system","definition":"A system that finds patterns from many examples instead of fixed rules."},{"term":"data","definition":"The examples or information a learning system is shown."},{"term":"model","definition":"The pattern a learning system builds from its data."},{"term":"example","definition":"One piece of data, like one photo or one email."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Two kinds of machine","body":["A [[rule-based system]] is like a recipe. A person writes every step, and the machine follows them exactly. A Salik toll gate charges you when your car passes - a person set that rule.","A [[learning system]] is different. Nobody writes a rule for every case. Instead it is shown many examples - this is [[data]] - and it finds the pattern by itself. The pattern it builds is called a [[model]]."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Why it matters","body":["If you know which kind a system is, you can guess when it might fail. A rule-based system fails when something happens that has no rule. A learning system can fail if it was shown poor or unfair examples.","Neither kind is magic, and neither understands like a person. That is why we always check what a machine tells us."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Time to be a detective. Sort three systems, then post the questions you most want answered this term."],"items":["Watch the two clips your teacher shows and spot which machine was told every step.","Sort the three cards into 'fixed rules' or 'learns from data'.","Write a reason under each card.","Post two questions on the class question wall.","Help agree one class rule for safe AI use."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which system was hardest to sort, and why?","What is one clue that a system learned from examples?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write one thing you now understand about how machines make decisions.","Write one question you still have."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 1 - Core - Worksheet | Unit Launch - Rule-Based vs Learning Systems","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w1-core-m-w1-core-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Sort three systems","prompt":"Write each system in the correct column and give one reason.","stem":"This follows fixed rules because ___\nThis learns from data because ___","lookFor":"Sorts at least 2 of the 3 systems correctly with a sensible reason. The traffic-light timer is fixed rules - it changes lights on a set timer that a person programmed; accept 'learns' only if the student describes a smart signal that adapts to traffic data. The spam-email filter learns from data - it was trained on many example emails marked spam or not spam, and no person wrote a rule for every email.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-core-m-w1-core-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"My two questions","prompt":"Write two genuine questions about rule-based and learning systems for the question wall.","lookFor":"Poses at least two genuine, on-topic questions, for example 'How many examples does a system need before it learns well?'. Any genuine, on-topic question counts - reward curiosity over neatness.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-core-m-w1-core-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"System sort record","prompt":"Complete the table for the three systems you sorted. For each row record: System | Fixed rules or learns from data | My reason.","lookFor":"Each row carries a reason, not a guess - press for where the logic comes from. Model rows: traffic-light timer, fixed rules, 'it changes lights on a set timer that a person programmed'; spam-email filter, learns from data, 'it was trained on many example emails marked spam or not spam'. Accept 'learns' for the traffic-light timer only if the student describes a smart signal that adapts to traffic data.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-core-m-w1-core-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Exit ticket","prompt":"In one sentence, how is a learning system different from a rule-based system?","lookFor":"Names where the logic comes from: a rule-based system does exactly what a person has written into it step by step, while a learning system is shown many examples and finds the pattern in that data. Watch for the misconception that a learning system is just a big set of fixed rules a programmer typed in.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-core-m-w1-core-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Challenge (stretch)","prompt":"Invent your own system card and swap with a partner - can they classify and justify it?","lookFor":"Invents a fourth system card that can genuinely be classified, and challenges another pair to classify and justify it. Strong responses can explain which clue in their own card settles the classification.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}},"g6-main-w1-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab","number":2,"week":1,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Rule vs Learning - Hands-On Exploration (Lab)","summary":"Working unplugged at two stations, students run a fixed rule-card machine and a learn-from-examples card game, log the differences and design a test that would reveal which kind an unknown system is.","duration":"45 minutes","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Explore a rule-based demo and a simple learning demo and log the differences you observe.","Devise a test that could tell whether a system follows rules or learns.","Predict what would break each system and check your prediction."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Today you get your hands on two machines - one that never changes and one that learns from examples. Watch closely: their differences will jump out."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can run the rule-card machine and the learn-from-examples game and record what each does.","I can log at least three differences I observed between them.","I can design a fair test that would reveal whether a system follows rules or learns."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"rule-card machine","definition":"A fixed stack of if-then cards that always behaves the same way."},{"term":"example card","definition":"A labelled card the group learns a pattern from."},{"term":"pattern","definition":"The rule-of-thumb your group builds from the example cards."},{"term":"test input","definition":"A new input you give a system to see how it behaves."},{"term":"predictable","definition":"Behaves the same way every time for the same input."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Two stations, two behaviours","body":["At Station A the [[rule-card machine]] never changes. Feed the same input twice and you get the same output twice. That is a rule-based system.","At Station B nobody gives you rules. You study [[example card]]s, build a [[pattern]], then classify new cards. That is a learning system in miniature."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Design a fair test","body":["To tell the two apart, give each a brand-new, unusual input. A rule-based machine reacts the same as always or breaks. A learning system tries to match the pattern it built.","The best detectives write down exactly what they will try and what each result would mean."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Run both stations, log the differences, then design a test that would reveal which kind an unknown machine is."],"items":["Take a role: feeder, recorder or tester.","Run Station A with five inputs, including one strange one.","Run Station B: study examples, then sort five new cards.","Log at least three differences.","Write one test that would separate rules from learning."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which station was more predictable, and how did you know?","What made the learning game guess wrongly?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write the clearest difference you saw today.","Write what you would test first on a mystery machine."]}],"worksheet":{"title":"Week 1 - Lab - Worksheet | Rule vs Learning - Hands-On Exploration (Lab)","questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab-m-w1-lab-q1","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Station comparison","prompt":"Log what each station did for the same kind of input.","stem":"Station A always ___\nStation B changed when ___","lookFor":"Records behaviour actually observed, e.g. 'Station A always gave the same output; Station B's guesses changed as we saw more example cards.' Any accurate observed difference is valid.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab-m-w1-lab-q2","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Design a test","prompt":"Write a test that would tell whether a system follows rules or learns, and what each result would mean.","lookFor":"Designs a test that would truly separate rules from learning: give the system a brand-new, unusual input; if it always reacts the same way it is rule-based, if it adapts using patterns it likely learned. Accept any test using a novel input to reveal adaptation; if the test does not separate the two, model one strong test and have the group revise.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab-m-w1-lab-q3","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Difference log","prompt":"Record the differences you observed between the two stations. For each row record: What we tried | Station A did | Station B did.","lookFor":"Logs at least three accurate differences with detail rather than one repeated observation. Look for the unusual input at Station A being noted: it had no rule for it, so it stopped or gave a wrong answer.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab-m-w1-lab-q4","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Exit ticket","prompt":"What one input would you give a mystery machine to find out if it learns? Why?","lookFor":"Chooses a brand-new or unusual input and says what each outcome would mean - the same reaction every time points to fixed rules, while an attempt to match a pattern points to learning. A named input with a reason beats a general statement about testing.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w1-lab-m-w1-lab-q5","type":"shortText","autoMarked":false,"title":"Challenge (stretch)","prompt":"Add an unfair set of example cards to Station B and explain how it changed the pattern the group learned.","lookFor":"Adds a deliberately unfair set of example cards and explains how it changed the learned pattern. Strong responses reach the idea that quality and fairness of examples matter, not just how many there are - a few odd or wrong cards can make the guesses worse.","evidenceType":"product","tierProbed":"emerging","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}},"g6-main-w10-core":{"id":"g6-main-w10-core","number":19,"week":10,"track":"main","type":"core","title":"Showcase, Assessment & Reflection","summary":"Learners present their finished solution with two justified choices, complete a short Term-1 assessment sampling all four strands, and set a goal for next term.","duration":"1 x 45-minute period","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Present the finished solution and explain at least two design/evaluation choices.","Demonstrate the term's key outcomes in a short assessment task.","State one thing learned and set one goal for next term."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["This is your moment to show what you built and what you learned. You will present your finished solution, explain the choices behind it, complete a short assessment, and set a goal to grow even more next term."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can present my finished solution and explain at least two design or evaluation choices.","I can show the term's key outcomes in a short assessment task.","I can state one thing I learned and set one goal for next term."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Pitch","definition":"A short, clear explanation of your solution and its value."},{"term":"Justify","definition":"To give the reason and evidence behind a choice."},{"term":"Assessment","definition":"A task that shows what you have learned across the strands."},{"term":"Reflection","definition":"Thinking about what worked and what you would do next."},{"term":"Goal","definition":"A clear target for your next step of learning."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"A pitch that tells the truth","body":["A strong [[pitch]] names your user, the problem, how your solution works, and the evidence that it is accurate, useful and safe.","Explain two choices by giving reasons, not just descriptions. Be honest about one limit. Honesty makes your work more trustworthy, not weaker."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Show the whole term, then look ahead","body":["The short [[assessment]] lets you show all four strands: understanding, building, evaluating and using responsibly, and wider effects.","Finish by naming one thing you learned and setting a [[goal]] for next term, aiming toward the Proficient tier."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Complete the short assessment, then present your solution and justify two choices before setting your next-term goal."],"items":["Set out your evidence from the term.","Complete the short assessment task on your own.","Prepare a 60-second pitch with two justified choices.","Present to your group and answer one 'why' question.","Write one thing learned and one Term-2 goal."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["Which of your two choices are you proudest of, and why?","What limit of your solution is important to be honest about?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write one thing you learned this term.","Set one goal for Term 2 that moves you toward Proficient."]}],"worksheet":{"questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w10-core-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"Write two design or evaluation choices and give a reason and evidence for each.","title":"My two justified choices","stem":"Choice 1: ... because ... evidence ...\nChoice 2: ... because ... evidence ...","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Explains two design/evaluation choices with reasons and evidence. For a design choice, look for a reason, not just a description (model: 'I used a rule-based check because recycling categories have fixed correct answers'). For an evaluation choice, it should link to accuracy or fairness (model: 'I tested with six known-answer cases because one lucky example is not enough evidence').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-core-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Answer the four short prompts, one for each strand, at Emerging level.","title":"Term-1 assessment task","stem":"Concepts: ...\nDesign & build: ...\nEvaluate & use: ...\nWider effects: ...","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Shows each strand at Emerging in the task. Approaching shows most strands at Emerging; not yet means several strands are not yet shown.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-core-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"For each strand, note your evidence and your confidence.","title":"Strand evidence tracker","stem":"Strand | My evidence | Confidence | Next step","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Evidence is the assessed task plus the reflection, with results reported per strand. Feedback flags each student's next tier target (to Proficient) for Term 2.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-core-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"One thing I learned this term is ... and my goal for next term is ...","title":"Exit ticket","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"States one learning and one clear next-term goal. Goal should aim toward Proficient (model: 'I learned to re-test after changes; my goal is to build a solution with balanced data next term').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-core-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Explain a trade-off you made between two choices and why it was worth it.","title":"Challenge (stretch)","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Stretch / next tier: learners explain a trade-off between two choices, reaching Extended abstract thinking.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}},"g6-main-w10-lab":{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab","number":20,"week":10,"track":"main","type":"lab","title":"Showcase Carousel and Reflection (Lab)","summary":"Learners run a showcase carousel, give and collect strand-tagged peer feedback, and consolidate the term into a four-strand Emerging summary with one Term-2 goal.","duration":"1 x 45-minute period","strands":["CU","SD","CE","GE"],"objectives":["Present the solution in a showcase carousel and give structured peer feedback.","Consolidate reflections into a Term-2 goal across the four strands.","Confirm the responsible-use message for every solution on display."],"sections":[{"type":"text","body":["Welcome to the showcase. Today your class becomes a gallery of AI-supported solutions. You will present, learn from each other with honest feedback, and pull your whole term together into one clear goal for next time."]},{"type":"list","heading":"I can…","items":["I can present my solution in a showcase carousel and give structured peer feedback.","I can consolidate my reflections into a Term-2 goal across the four strands.","I can confirm my solution is responsible to use and honest about its limits."]},{"type":"vocabulary","heading":"Words to know","terms":[{"term":"Carousel","definition":"A rotation where you present at your station and visit others."},{"term":"Two stars and a wish","definition":"Two things done well and one thing to improve."},{"term":"Consolidate","definition":"To gather many notes into one clear summary."},{"term":"Responsible use","definition":"No personal data, honest about limits, fair to users."},{"term":"Proficient","definition":"The next tier of skill you aim for in Term 2."}]},{"type":"text","heading":"Feedback that helps","body":["In the [[carousel]] you present in 60 seconds and then visit other stations. Leave '[[two stars and a wish]]', and tag each comment to a strand.","Good feedback is specific, kind and tied to evidence. A helpful wish is a gift, not a criticism."]},{"type":"text","heading":"Your term in one picture","body":["Gather your feedback and notes into the four-strand summary: what you can now do in concepts, design and build, evaluate and use, and wider effects.","Then set one specific Term-2 goal toward [[Proficient]], and confirm every solution is responsible to use."]},{"type":"activity","label":"Let's try it - hands-on","heading":"Let's try it - hands-on","body":["Set up your station, present in the carousel, give and collect feedback, then consolidate your term into a four-strand summary and one goal."],"items":["Set up your station with your frozen solution, evidence and responsible-use message.","Present in 60 seconds with two justified choices.","Rotate to at least two stations and leave strand-tagged feedback.","Collect the feedback left at your station.","Complete the four-strand Emerging summary.","Set one Term-2 goal and confirm responsible use."]},{"type":"list","heading":"Think about it","items":["What is the most useful wish someone gave you, and why?","How will you keep your future solutions responsible and fair?"]},{"type":"list","heading":"My reflection","items":["Write your four-strand summary, one line per strand.","Set one specific Term-2 goal that moves you toward Proficient."]}],"worksheet":{"questions":[{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab-q1","type":"shortText","prompt":"For two peers, write two stars and a wish, each tagged to a strand.","title":"Carousel feedback slips","stem":"Star (strand): ...\nStar (strand): ...\nWish (strand): ...","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Gives specific 'two stars and a wish' tagged to strands. A star must name a strand and evidence (model: 'Star (Evaluate & use): you tested with six known-answer cases, which is strong evidence'). A wish should be specific and kind (model: 'Wish (Wider effects): explain who might be treated unfairly and how you would prevent it').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab-q2","type":"shortText","prompt":"Write one Emerging statement per strand, then set one Term-2 goal.","title":"Four-strand Emerging summary and goal","stem":"Concepts: I can ...\nDesign & build: I can ...\nEvaluate & use: I can ...\nWider effects: I can ...\nTerm-2 goal: ...","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Summarises all four strands at Emerging with evidence - one clause per strand at Emerging (model: 'I can explain rule-based vs learning, build a solution, evaluate it for risk, and consider wider effects'). The goal should be specific and tied to a strand toward Proficient (model: 'Next term I will use balanced data so my solution is fairer to all users').","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab-q3","type":"shortText","prompt":"For each strand, record your Emerging evidence and next-term focus.","title":"End-of-term reflection tracker","stem":"Strand | Emerging evidence | Feedback received | Term-2 focus","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Evidence is the feedback slips plus the completed four-strand Emerging summary with goal. Teacher flags each learner's next-tier target for Term 2.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab-q4","type":"shortText","prompt":"My proudest strand this term is ... and my Term-2 goal toward Proficient is ...","title":"Exit ticket","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Sets a specific goal and confirms responsible use; setting a goal or confirming responsible use but not both is only Approaching.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]},{"id":"g6-main-w10-lab-q5","type":"shortText","prompt":"Combine feedback from several peers into one improved design idea to try in Term 2, and explain your choice.","title":"Challenge (stretch)","autoMarked":false,"lookFor":"Stretch / next tier: learners synthesise feedback from several peers into one improved design idea for Term 2.","frameworkRefs":[{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CU","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CU·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"SD","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·SD·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"CE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·CE·G6·E"},{"framework":"AIF","strand":"GE","grade":6,"tier":"E","code":"AIF·GE·G6·E"}]}]}}}};
